.Dd $Mdocdate: August 1 2026$
.Dt OPENBAR.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openbar.conf
.Nd configuration file for openbar
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the configuration file for
.Xr openbar 1 .
It controls which system information is displayed on the
status bar.
.Pp
The file may be placed at
.Pa ~/.openbar.conf
.Pq per-user
or
.Pa /etc/openbar.conf
.Pq system-wide .
If both exist the per-user file takes precedence.
.Pp
A custom path may be specified with the
.Fl c
option of
.Xr openbar 1 .
.Sh SYNTAX
Each line is a
.Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value
pair.
Boolean features accept
.Dq yes
or
.Dq no .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar logo
Displayed text or name.
Example:
.Dl logo=OpenBar
.It Ar date
Display the current date and time.
.It Ar cpu
Display CPU speed and temperature.
.It Ar bat
Display battery status and percentage.
.It Ar mem
Display free memory in MB.
.It Ar load
Display the 1-minute load average.
.It Ar net
Display public and private IP addresses.
Public addresses are fetched from
.Pa ifconfig.me
by a sandboxed network worker process.
.It Ar hostname
Display the system hostname.
.It Ar interface
Network interface used to obtain the internal IP address.
Example:
.Dl interface=iwm0
.It Ar vpn
Display whether a WireGuard
.Pq wg
interface is active.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.openbar.conf
Per-user configuration.
.It Pa /etc/openbar.conf
System-wide configuration.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
logo=openbar
date=yes
cpu=yes
bat=yes
mem=yes
load=yes
net=yes
hostname=yes
interface=iwm0
vpn=yes
.Ed
.Sh SECURITY
The enabled features directly affect the
.Xr pledge 2
promise set retained by the main process during
steady-state operation.
Enabling
.Ar bat
adds
.Dq rpath ioctl
.Po for
.Pa /dev/apm
.Pc ,
.Ar cpu
or
.Ar mem
adds
.Dq sysctl ,
and
.Ar vpn
or
.Ar net
adds
.Dq route
.Po for
.Xr getifaddrs 3
.Pc .
Disabling unneeded features reduces the authority available
to a compromised main process.
.Pp
The network worker is always forked when
.Ar net
is enabled and runs under an independent sandbox with
.Dq stdio inet dns
and filesystem visibility limited to DNS resolution
files.
.Pp
The configuration file path must be unveiled before
the
.Xr unveil 2
lock; late access to undeclared paths is rejected with a
diagnostic.
All paths listed here require runtime verification
on a real
.Ox
system.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openbar 1 ,
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Xr unveil 2
